  "body": "KapKan 1.0.6 updates macOS voice-chat microphone capability and the managed runtime, and reduces repeated HUD/render work.\r\n\r\nUse the exact Minecraft 26.1, 26.1.1 or 26.1.2 build with Java 25 and Fabric Loader 0.19.5+. Desktop packages include all three builds. Existing worlds, mods, controls and graphics preferences are preserved.\r\n\r\nOptional ImmediatelyFast rendering optimizations are included with their licenses and exact corresponding sources. Existing user copies and declared conflicts take precedence. Settings \u2192 Game performance \u2192 Use rendering optimizations applies on the next game start.\r\n\r\nAll three builds pass 1,209 deterministic checks each and native macOS arm64 world-entry checks with the selected rendering addition and verified Zulu25 runtime. The final module integration passes 56 checks. Launcher/Fabric recovery, real 1.0.5 migration, installer payload and archive checks pass. The Mac app signature/audio capability and clean Java 21/25 runtime installation were verified.\r\n\r\nThe Mac app is locally signed and not Developer ID notarized; Windows is unsigned. Interactive microphone consent/capture and native Windows installation remain untested. macOS approval stays under your control when voice chat opens input.\r\n\r\nClose KapKan and Minecraft before replacing the app. Keep the complete portable Windows folder together. SHA256SUMS.txt lists every binary."
